1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,397
Hello everyone.

2
00:00:01,397 --> 00:00:07,258
We are presenting Sentinel, an AI powered citizen incident reporting and intelligent

3
00:00:07,258 --> 00:00:09,073
emergency dispatch system.

4
00:00:09,073 --> 00:00:15,283
It was developed by Latheshkumar, Madesh, Jeffrin and Kamalesh Balaji, under the guidance

5
00:00:15,283 --> 00:00:15,702
of Ms.

6
00:00:15,702 --> 00:00:19,330
Sumitha T, for the Product Development Lab at R.M.K.

7
00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:20,726
Engineering College.

8
00:00:21,683 --> 00:00:27,840
Today, when a citizen in Chennai sees a fire, an accident or a flooded road, the only

9
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:31,099
option is to call a helpline and describe it.

10
00:00:31,099 --> 00:00:33,924
A phone call carries no photo or video.

11
00:00:33,924 --> 00:00:36,314
The location is a vague landmark.

12
00:00:36,314 --> 00:00:40,371
One visible incident triggers dozens of duplicate calls.

13
00:00:40,371 --> 00:00:45,875
And calls are handled in the order they arrive, not by how serious they are.

14
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:49,657
Sentinel fixes this in three steps.

15
00:00:49,657 --> 00:00:54,148
Citizens report with evidence and an exact GPS location.

16
00:00:54,148 --> 00:01:00,563
An AI pipeline verifies, summarises, de-duplicates and prioritises every report.

17
00:01:00,563 --> 00:01:06,578
And dispatchers see a live map and send the nearest responder in one click.

18
00:01:07,528 --> 00:01:09,592
The system has four tiers.

19
00:01:09,592 --> 00:01:14,118
A React progressive web app for citizens and dispatchers.

20
00:01:14,118 --> 00:01:19,119
A FastAPI backend with secure login and live WebSocket updates.

21
00:01:19,119 --> 00:01:21,501
PostgreSQL and Redis for data.

22
00:01:21,501 --> 00:01:26,344
And an AI worker that runs every report through the pipeline.

23
00:01:27,295 --> 00:01:33,490
The pipeline runs YOLO version 8 on photos and video frames, checks the photo's EXIF data

24
00:01:33,490 --> 00:01:38,503
against the reported location, and transcribes voice notes with Whisper.

25
00:01:38,503 --> 00:01:44,559
A Qwen 3.5 language model, running locally through llama dot c p p, extracts the hazard

26
00:01:44,559 --> 00:01:46,578
type, severity and a summary.

27
00:01:46,578 --> 00:01:52,565
Sentence embeddings and a Union Find algorithm merge duplicate reports, and a weighted

28
00:01:52,565 --> 00:01:54,236
score sets the priority.

29
00:01:54,236 --> 00:01:59,527
If any model is missing, Sentinel records that honestly instead of guessing.

30
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:02,163
Let us see it working.

31
00:02:02,163 --> 00:02:08,761
A citizen opens Sentinel on their phone, chooses Road Accident, and describes what they

32
00:02:08,761 --> 00:02:10,733
see at Kathipara junction.

33
00:02:10,733 --> 00:02:16,951
They attach a photo, and tap Use my location to fill in the exact GPS coordinates.

34
00:02:16,951 --> 00:02:18,999
One tap submits the report.

35
00:02:19,695 --> 00:02:24,663
The report is saved instantly and the citizen receives a tracking ID.

36
00:02:24,663 --> 00:02:29,631
In the background, the AI pipeline has already started working on it.

37
00:02:30,195 --> 00:02:35,521
With the tracking ID, the citizen can follow the report through seven stages, from

38
00:02:35,521 --> 00:02:39,939
Reported, through AI Processing and Verified, all the way to Closed.

39
00:02:41,095 --> 00:02:43,004
Now the dispatcher signs in.

40
00:02:43,004 --> 00:02:48,800
The dashboard shows every active incident across Chennai, from Ennore in the north to

41
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,301
Tambaram in the south.

42
00:02:50,301 --> 00:02:56,370
The cards at the top show incidents by severity, available units, and duplicate clusters.

43
00:02:56,370 --> 00:03:02,370
The heat map highlights where incidents are concentrated, and the live feed on the right

44
00:03:02,370 --> 00:03:03,871
is sorted by priority.

45
00:03:04,428 --> 00:03:06,876
Here is the report we just submitted.

46
00:03:06,876 --> 00:03:12,433
YOLO detected the bus and the people in the photo, and the language model turned the

47
00:03:12,433 --> 00:03:18,255
citizen's words into a structured record: a road accident at Kathipara junction, needing

48
00:03:18,255 --> 00:03:21,364
an immediate response, with a one line summary.

49
00:03:21,364 --> 00:03:24,804
The provenance block shows exactly which models ran.

50
00:03:25,498 --> 00:03:28,758
This transformer fire on Ranganathan Street in T.

51
00:03:28,758 --> 00:03:32,150
Nagar was reported three times by different people.

52
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:36,940
Sentinel merged the reports into one cluster, which raised its priority.

53
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:41,729
The k d tree lists the nearest available responders with their distance.

54
00:03:41,729 --> 00:03:47,516
Officer Priya Nair from Fire and Rescue is only a hundred and fifty metres away, so the

55
00:03:47,516 --> 00:03:52,306
dispatcher sends her with one click, and the status moves to Dispatched.

56
00:03:52,865 --> 00:03:58,451
The analytics page shows the category and status breakdown, available units, duplicate

57
00:03:58,451 --> 00:04:04,297
clusters, and the average time to dispatch and to resolve, so the control room can measure

58
00:04:04,297 --> 00:04:05,921
and improve its response.

59
00:04:07,231 --> 00:04:12,716
On our Chennai dataset of eighteen reports, all three duplicate groups were merged

60
00:04:12,716 --> 00:04:18,401
correctly, and each report was triaged in about seven seconds on a single laptop GPU.

61
00:04:18,401 --> 00:04:23,551
The project has one hundred and eleven automated tests, and all of them pass.

62
00:04:24,501 --> 00:04:30,133
In the future, Sentinel can be connected to the 112 emergency response system, support

63
00:04:30,133 --> 00:04:36,027
Tamil and other languages, and add a responder mobile app and flood hotspot prediction for

64
00:04:36,027 --> 00:04:36,813
the monsoon.

65
00:04:37,768 --> 00:04:39,736
Thank you for watching.

